  "behavior": [
    "SPU, SID and DMG adapters use one ordered project-store layer over the FM reconnect helper. Complete operations, including one lifecycle retry, retain arrival order and detached snapshots.",
    "The original per-app database names, schema version 1, projects/current key, typed binary snapshots and localStorage keys/$spuBytes/$sidBytes/$dmgBytes fallback encodings are unchanged.",
    "Closed/version-changing connections reopen without replaying application restoration. A failed initial open is not cached permanently against later I/O.",
    "Persistence starts only after successful initial read and validation. Failed or invalid stored projects are never replaced with defaults or later edits; current in-memory files remain exportable.",
    "Shared Code flush captures workspace/path/source before awaiting persistence. An older commit cannot clear a newer recovery journal; this common correction also applies to FM2612.",
    "SID and DMG retain sound edits made during a slow successful initial read and schedule their save after restoration.",
    "Close drains accepted writes and rejects late operations without reopening a disposed store. No database deletion, schema migration, automatic localStorage downgrade or public API/DSP change.",
    "Entry and transitive frontend cache identities are updated. Readable helper modules and matching adapters are included in the three standalone distributions; workflows run the muted storage fault checker."
